# Vue-Specific Formatting Guidelines

This project follows the [Vue.js Style Guide](mdc:https:/v2.vuejs.org/v2/style-guide) with an emphasis on the following rules.

## Component Structure

Components should follow this structure:
1. `<template>`
2. `<script>`
3. `<style>`

Within the `<script>` section, organize component properties in this order:
```js
export default {
  name: 'ComponentName',
  
  components: {},
  
  mixins: [],
  
  props: {},
  
  data () {
    return {}
  },
  
  computed: {},
  
  watch: {},
  
  created () {},
  
  mounted () {},
  
  methods: {}
}
```

## Component Naming

- Use multi-word names for components to avoid conflicts with HTML elements
- Use PascalCase for component definitions: `MyComponent.vue`
- Use kebab-case in templates: `<my-component>`

## Props

- Always use camelCase for prop names in JavaScript
- Use kebab-case in templates
- Be detailed in prop definitions:

```js
props: {
  status: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
    validator: (value) => ['success', 'warning', 'error'].includes(value)
  },
  message: {
    type: String,
    default: ''
  }
}
```

## Events

- Use kebab-case for event names: `this.$emit('item-selected')`
- Emit a value with events when useful: `this.$emit('item-selected', item)`

## Template Syntax

- Use directives shorthand:
  - `:` for `v-bind`
  - `@` for `v-on`
- Indent content inside template tags properly
- Multi-line attributes should each be on their own line:

```vue
<component
  :prop1="value1"
  :prop2="value2"
  @event="handleEvent"
>
  Content
</component>
```

## Style Guidelines

- Use scoped styles when appropriate: `<style scoped>`
- Use SCSS when needed: `<style lang="scss">`
- Follow BEM naming convention for CSS classes when possible
- Consistent spacing in CSS:

```css
.my-class {
  property: value;
  other-property: other-value;
}
```

## Vuex Usage

- Use namespaced modules
- Use mapState, mapGetters, mapActions, mapMutations helpers appropriately
- Structure Vuex store properly with actions, mutations, and getters
